# Build context exclusions for examples/dev-fixture/Dockerfile only.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the repository root's
# `.dockerignore` when it exists, and it does not merge the two. This file
# exists because the root list excludes `examples`, which the fixture image has
# to copy; everything else below is the root list restated, because dropping it
# would let a developer's node_modules and secrets into the context.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.claude
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
deploy/compose/secrets
docs
*.log

# The fixture image builds the connector from source and installs both
# applications. Nothing else under examples/ belongs in the context: the agent
# instruction examples are documentation, not something this image runs.
#
# `examples/dev-fixture/vite-app` is deliberately NOT excluded: the
# `vite-app-builder` stage installs its dependencies from the committed
# `package-lock.json` and copies its sources. `**/node_modules` above still
# excludes a developer's local install from the context either way — the
# image only ever gets the `npm ci` it runs for itself.
examples/claude-code
examples/opencode
